# OAuth client id for Drive sync. Not a secret: it identifies the app, and
# Google enforces which origins may present it. A build without it says so in
# the info panel rather than offering a button that cannot work.
#
# Create at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials with the Drive
# API enabled and these authorized JavaScript origins:
#   https://hikarintu.github.io
#   http://localhost:5173
#
# The name matters: Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to client
# code, so a plain CLIENT_ID is read by nothing and the app reports itself
# unconfigured with the value sitting right there.
#
# Never give the client *secret* a VITE_ prefix, or any other route into this
# file. The token flow does not use one, and a VITE_ variable is inlined into
# public JavaScript at build time.
#
# Copy to .env, which is gitignored.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
